{
	title: 'Persistent scheduled unattended jobs',
	spec: 'Hal provides /schedule list/show/add/edit/pause/resume/run/stop/remove in the shared command transcript, not a separate screen. Jobs persist normalized timing, prompt, creation cwd, user timezone, model (default and openai/claude resolved each run or exact pin), fresh/continue history, optional timeout and autoclose. Direct dependency-free timing supports durations (30m, every hour), hourly at :20/every :30, weekdays at times, daily time lists and inclusive ranges such as 09:00..19:00 every 1h, including unambiguous ellipsis syntax. Clock schedules match real timestamps in the saved user timezone: repeated fall-back minutes both occur, missing spring minutes skip. No overlapping runs of one job; occurrences while active skip, different jobs run concurrently. One catchup after downtime; uncertain interrupted runs are recorded and never retried automatically. Runs use ordinary unattended turns, tools and plugins including hal/tool; cwd grants no trust, and continued jobs respect revoked trust. Human takeover disables timeout and autoclose. Routine success is quiet, failures persist visibly. Job changes are visible and attributed. /schedule lists all running/waiting/paused jobs with prompt summary, timing, current or last clickable session/tab, next timestamp and timezone; /schedule ID shows all settings and past runs. Missing arguments use shared guided forms or ASON. Completion includes operations and enumerable values. Tests cover timing, DST, lifecycle, recovery and trust boundaries.',
